OL,3,GNEWSAHow 1930s nobility rewarded their
OL,4,Aservants at Christmas
OL,5,
OL,6,FIf you were to step inside the lower
OL,7,Ffloors of a stately home 100 years ago,
OL,8,Fyou would see the corridors buzzing
OL,9,Fwith servants.
OL,11,FWhile staff numbers at many residences
OL,12,Fshrunk post-World War One, at Ickworth
OL,13,FHouse, near Bury St Edmunds, Suffolk,
OL,14,Fnumerous people were still serving the
OL,15,Ffourth Marquess and Marchioness of
OL,16,FBristol in the mid-1930s.
OL,18,FAt Christmas time, the workload in
OL,19,Fstately homes often ramped up for the
OL,20,Fservants with little time for
OL,21,Frelaxation or celebration of their own.
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,380,370,200,160,0,100
